## Commit / Git Attribution Guardrail (Critical)

When suggesting or generating commits, branch names, or PR descriptions during any agent session (especially execute-plan, split-to-prs, git-worktrees, or long-running plans):

- **Never** inject boilerplate or attribution from other LLMs (e.g. "Generated with Claude Code", "Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>", Cursor-specific strings) unless the user has explicitly confirmed they are using that LLM/tool in the current context on this machine.
- Default to clean, factual commit messages only.
- If any form of attribution feels appropriate, ask the user first ("Do you want any agent attribution in the commit message?").
- This mistake has previously caused significant user confusion when the user had never installed or used the other LLM.

This rule applies especially strongly in Grok-native sessions (`/fusion-sage`, `execute-plan`, this CLI environment).

Never do one without considering the other. The best answers come from running the fission engine first, then igniting the fusion reactor on top.

